&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-146&quot; title=&quot;Force IE to use &amp;quot;edge&amp;quot; compatible mode&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;ZEPPELIN-146&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;ZEPPELIN-146&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; Force IE to use &quot;edge&quot; compatible mode&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-146&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-146&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    In Microsoft internal deployment, compatible level of IE will be set to &quot;5&quot; for interant sites, due to group policy set by admin.&lt;br/&gt;
    Then, some JavaScript will be broken, and home page of Zeppelin cannot be rendered.&lt;br/&gt;
    We need to set X-UA-Compatible tag for IE to &quot;edge&quot; to force it use the latest IE version.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You can merge this pull request into a Git repository by running:&lt;/p&gt;

